WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.610
The idea of socialism
has become very popular

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:03.434
among young people.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.850
And the reason that it's become
popular among young people

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.920
is, because they've been
told that it is moral.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.170
Not that it works, not that
it's great, but that it's moral.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:10.799
It's fair.

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:12.340
And we all like
things that are fair.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.890
If we're in a room and
somebody has more money,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.090
and somebody has less
money, wouldn't it

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.010
be more fair if we
just pooled the money--

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.410
and then we split it up
evenly among the participants?

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.411
You know, just like the
cookies in kindergarten.

00:00:21.411 --> 00:00:23.618
Except of course, that's
not the way the world works,

00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:25.020
and that's not actually moral.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.050
Because in a free country,
wealth, and the capacity

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.540
to gain it, is largely
contingent on the decisions

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.680
that you make.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.337
It doesn't just fall upon you.

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:35.420
Most wealth in the United
States is not inherited.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.630
Most wealth in the
United States is

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.171
created over the
course of lifetimes,

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.490
by people who engage in
economic activity and commerce.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.100
Capitalism is good, because
capitalism is freedom.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.860
Socialism is bad, because
socialism is tyranny.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.240
Not an aspect of tyranny--

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.160
socialism itself is tyranny.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.290
The statement of socialism
is, that your labor

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.339
is owed to the society.

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:56.130
The notion of socialism
is, that you do not

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.030
own your own freedom.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.470
You do not own your own time.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.760
You do not own your own labor.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.050
You do not own your own work.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.940
You do not own the
products of your own work.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.319
The basic notion
of capitalism is,

00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:05.459
you own all of those things.

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.260
And now you have to
engage in free exchange

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.200
with someone else who
does not owe you anything.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.370
If you want to thrive,
if you want to succeed,

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.120
you are going to have to make
something somebody else wants.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.000
People think capitalism
is selfishness.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.260
No, socialism is
selfishness-- the notion

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.210
that I have to
somehow supply you

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.040
the money so you can
sit in your basement

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.559
and paint with watercolors.

00:01:24.559 --> 00:01:26.100
Socialism, the idea
that I'm supposed

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.070
to fulfill all your dreams
by paying you for something I

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.790
don't want, and
have no need for.

